          "type": "html",
          "html": "<div class=\"kicker\">05</div>\n<h2>Before you start</h2>\n<p>Do this when you both have some capacity for it. A morning. An afternoon. A weekend.</p>\n<p>It may well not be at night. At the end of a long day, you may both have less attention available for something that asks you to really listen.</p>\n<p>Give the fifteen minutes a little bit of space.</p>\n<ol class=\"steps\">\n<li><span class=\"n\">1</span><div><b>Phones away</b><p>Phones in another room. Keep one only for the timer and prompt.</p></div></li>\n<li><span class=\"n\">2</span><div><b>Face each other</b><p>Sit or stand facing each other. Take one breath in through the nose and out through the mouth, together.</p></div></li>\n<li><span class=\"n\">3</span><div><b>Look at each other</b><p>You might laugh. Look away. Want to make a joke of it.</p><p class=\"quiet\">Let that happen. Notice it. It is information, not a wrong start.</p></div></li>\n<li><span class=\"n\">4</span><div><b>Decide who is A and who is B</b><p>Set your timer for fifteen minutes. Begin.</p></div></li>\n</ol>\n<h3>The fifteen minutes</h3>\n<div class=\"ab\"><div><b>A</b><span>asks the prompt</span></div><div><b>B</b><span>answers first</span></div></div>\n<p>A asks the prompt. Out loud, exactly as written.</p>\n<p>B takes a breath and lets it land. Then B gives one clear communication.</p>\n<p>Not a speech. One thing, honestly, from wherever the question lands for them.</p>\n<p>A responds with one of the three answers. Thank You. Clarify That. Summarise That. Nothing else.</p>\n<p>If A says Clarify That or Summarise That, B responds to that. A listens again.</p>\n<p>When A reaches Thank You, you swap. Same prompt. Now B asks and A speaks.</p>\n<div class=\"loop\"><span>One communication.</span><span class=\"ar\">→</span><span>Receive it.</span><span class=\"ar\">→</span><span>Thank You.</span><span class=\"ar\">→</span><span>Swap.</span></div>\n<p>Back and forth with the same prompt until the timer goes.</p>\n<h3>The rules that make it work</h3>\n<ul class=\"rules\">\n<li>No fixing.</li><li>No defending.</li><li>No interrupting.</li><li>No debating.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Do not ride on each other's communication.</p>\n<p>When it's your turn, don't answer what they just said or continue their thread.</p>\n<p class=\"lead\">Your turn is your own.</p>\n<p>Take the same prompt fresh and notice where it lands for you.</p>\n<p>There is no correct answer. There is only what is present for you right now.</p>\n<p>Stay with the same prompt for the full fifteen minutes. You may think you've already answered it. Ask it again.</p>\n<p>Your first answer isn't necessarily your only answer.</p>\n<p>When the timer goes, finish the communication you're in, reach Thank You, and stop.</p>\n<p class=\"big\">That's the whole structure.</p>\n<p class=\"lead\" style=\"margin-top:30px\">Before you start</p>"
