          "html": "<div class=\"kicker\">07</div>\n<h2>Afterwards</h2>\n<p>When the timer goes, finish the communication you're in and reach Thank You. Then stop.</p>\n<ul class=\"rules\">\n<li>Don't immediately discuss what was said.</li>\n<li>Don't analyse it.</li>\n<li>Don't ask, \"When you said that, did you mean...?\"</li>\n<li>Don't start explaining your side now that the fifteen minutes are over.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>You have just spent fifteen minutes practising letting one another's communication land without fixing, defending or debating it.</p>\n<p class=\"big\">Let it <em>land.</em></p>\n<p>You don't need to do anything with it straight away. Leave it alone for now.</p>\n<p>Let the conversation have some space before you decide whether anything else needs to be said.</p>\n<h3>What you might notice</h3>\n<p>At first, the structure might feel a little wooden.</p>\n<p>You may be concentrating on remembering the three answers. You may forget and start responding normally. You may want to explain, defend, fix, reassure or ask another question.</p>\n<p>Notice it. Then come back to the structure.</p>\n<p>You may also notice that when the same prompt comes back to you, your answer changes.</p>\n<p>Something you were certain you'd finished with suddenly has something else underneath it.</p>\n<p>Or you hear yourself say something you hadn't realised was there until you said it out loud.</p>\n<p class=\"lead\">And some days?</p>\n<p>Nothing dramatic happens at all. You answer the question. Your partner answers the question. The timer goes.</p>\n<p>That counts too.</p>\n<p>The point isn't to manufacture a breakthrough. You're practising a different way of communicating:</p>\n<ul class=\"dots\">\n<li>Speaking one clear thing.</li>\n<li>Receiving one clear thing.</li>\n<li>Not immediately doing something with what you've heard.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Over these seven sittings, the structure may start to feel more familiar.</p>\n<p class=\"big\">Thank You. Clarify That. Summarise That.</p>\n<p>They become three moves you know how to reach for when an ordinary conversation starts disappearing underneath explaining, defending and fixing.</p>\n<p>That's what we're practising.</p>\n<div class=\"faq\">\n<h3>If you lose the structure</h3>\n<p>You probably will at some point. That's okay.</p>\n<details>\n<summary><span>One of you starts defending, explaining or debating.</span><span class=\"pl\">+</span></summary>\n<div class=\"dbody\"><p>Pause. You don't need to analyse what happened. Just name it:</p><p>\"We've left the three answers. Let's come back.\"</p><p>Then come back to the prompt and the structure.</p></div>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary><span>One of you gets emotional.</span><span class=\"pl\">+</span></summary>\n<div class=\"dbody\"><p>Emotion doesn't automatically mean you need to stop. It doesn't mean you have to keep going either.</p><p>Take a moment. The person speaking gets to decide whether they want to continue or whether they need to stop.</p><p>You don't need to immediately soothe them, pull more out of them or make the feeling go away.</p><p>But the structure never overrides someone's wish to pause or stop.</p></div>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary><span>It turns into a row.</span><span class=\"pl\">+</span></summary>\n<div class=\"dbody\"><p>Stop the timer. Don't try to rescue the Dyad by forcing yourselves through the remaining minutes.</p><p>Come back to it another day.</p><p>Stopping cleanly is better than using the structure to keep a conversation going when neither of you is actually in it anymore.</p></div>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary><span>Your partner doesn't want to do it.</span><span class=\"pl\">+</span></summary>\n<div class=\"dbody\"><p>Do the solo version. Choose the 10-minute timer, take today's prompt and use it as mind clearing.</p><p>You don't need somebody else's participation to begin practising how you communicate.</p></div>\n</details>\n</div>\n<div class=\"endcard\">\n<p class=\"big\" style=\"margin:0\">The structure is there to support the conversation. <em>It isn't another rule you have to get right.</em></p>\n</div>"
